"""Independent meanings from complete clean Japanese exchanges; no earlier English consulted."""
CONTEXT={
0:'Maria and her companions debate the purpose and possible authenticity of the sought-after Proofs. Western domination is criticized, but fabrication remains a suggestion challenged by a conditional counterargument. Separate spokesperson branches are not assumed to be spoken together. Maria resolves to find the treasures before the powers can exploit them.',
1:'Yukihisa identifies the named blade and describes its unsettling appearance. Preserve the legendary epithet without asserting an actual magical gameplay effect.',
2:'Gerhard recognizes a previously relinquished, unnamed object by its unchanged dull gleam. The source does not explain how he parted with it or name a prior owner.',
3:'Kurushima challenges Maria and quarrels with Yukihisa about samurai honor and plundering defenseless coastal people. His coercive offer is rejected with a threat to his beard, after which he threatens murder. Ane-san is a rough address, not a family relationship. The surrender permission and only-you life-saving threat concern Maria, not Kurushima surrendering himself.',
4:'Maria demands that Escante release the people under his unjust colonial rule. He dresses his own planned independence and appropriation of New World wealth as liberation; Maria rejects that self-serving rationale. His sexist/childish insults are condescension, not evidence of her age. Hodram offers unsolicited aid against their shared enemy in a later passage; no romance or new allegiance is invented.',
5:'Aziza identifies the encroaching FO fleet and assigns command, maneuvering and gunnery to Snake, Angel and Dandy. Her excitement is battle swagger, not an invented sexual relationship. Maria and Xien discuss the unusual female pirate and prepare to confront piracy. Preserve the full faction macro as a faction identity, avoiding an invented second fleet belonging to that fleet.',
6:'Aziza challenges the recurring rival. Preserve the FO target and her confident threat; separate conditional exchanges are not necessarily one uninterrupted speech.',
7:'Maria confronts Yuris as a ship thief. He indignantly claims elite noble birth; that is his claim, not an endorsement by the narration. Maria teases his sensitivity and threatens to send him to Batavia without inventing his punishment.',
8:'Maria confronts Jacob Portunto over an illicit trader turning to piracy; he rejects her lecture. Preserve the taunt and warning without adding an unmentioned specific smuggled cargo or conviction.',
9:'Maria rebukes Gabriel for violating an agreement. He dismisses agreements, she threatens to make him understand by force, and he welcomes the challenge.',
10:'William Clive delivers an exaggerated, threatening pirate cackle. Maria responds with dry disbelief; his animal-like cries do not establish that he is literally an animal.',
}
